---
/** The architecture, as a figure: the model, the crates, and what comes out. */
---

<figure class="mt-pipeline not-content" aria-labelledby="mt-pipeline-caption">
	<ol class="mt-pipeline__row">
		<li class="mt-pipeline__stage mt-pipeline__stage--source">
			<span class="mt-pipeline__kicker">The model</span>
			<span class="mt-pipeline__name">doc.json</span>
			<span class="mt-pipeline__note">sections, pages, spreads, styles, masters, components</span>
		</li>
		<li class="mt-pipeline__stage">
			<span class="mt-pipeline__kicker">matenadar-model</span>
			<span class="mt-pipeline__name">Validate &amp; change</span>
			<span class="mt-pipeline__note">JSON paths in errors, components, reversible operations. No Typst.</span>
		</li>
		<li class="mt-pipeline__stage">
			<span class="mt-pipeline__kicker">matenadar-typst</span>
			<span class="mt-pipeline__name">Generate &amp; lay out</span>
			<span class="mt-pipeline__note">a Typst program on every build, never stored; inspection and checks</span>
		</li>
		<li class="mt-pipeline__stage mt-pipeline__stage--out">
			<span class="mt-pipeline__kicker">Out</span>
			<span class="mt-pipeline__name">PDF · SVG · PNG</span>
			<span class="mt-pipeline__note">and, through <code>matenadar-epub</code>, EPUB&nbsp;3</span>
		</li>
	</ol>
	<p class="mt-pipeline__wasm">
		<span class="mt-pipeline__kicker">matenadar-wasm · @matenadar/wasm</span>
		The same engine as WebAssembly, in browsers, workers, Node, Bun and Deno, with the same pages (<code>fingerprint</code>).
	</p>
	<figcaption id="mt-pipeline-caption">
		The model is the only source of truth: the command line, the page editor and agents all change books through it.
	</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.mt-pipeline {
		margin: 2rem 0 2.5rem;
	}
	.mt-pipeline__row {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}
	.mt-pipeline__stage {
		position: relative;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.3rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0.9rem 1rem 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--mt-border);
		border-radius: 12px;
		background: var(--mt-surface);
		box-shadow: var(--mt-shadow-sm);
	}
	.mt-pipeline__stage + .mt-pipeline__stage::before {
		content: '→';
		position: absolute;
		left: -0.72rem;
		top: 50%;
		transform: translateY(-50%);
		width: 0.7rem;
		text-align: center;
		color: var(--mt-fg-faint);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
	.mt-pipeline__stage--out {
		border-color: var(--mt-accent-ring);
		background: var(--mt-accent-soft);
	}
	.mt-pipeline__kicker {
		font-family: var(--mt-mono);
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		color: var(--mt-accent-text);
	}
	.mt-pipeline__name {
		font-size: 1rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		line-height: 1.25;
		color: var(--mt-fg);
	}
	.mt-pipeline__stage--source .mt-pipeline__name {
		font-family: var(--mt-mono);
		font-size: 0.92rem;
	}
	.mt-pipeline__note {
		font-size: 0.8125rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: var(--mt-fg-muted);
	}
	.mt-pipeline__wasm {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.2rem 0.75rem;
		align-items: baseline;
		margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
		padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
		border: 1px dashed var(--mt-border-strong);
		border-radius: 12px;
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		color: var(--mt-fg-muted);
	}
	.mt-pipeline code {
		font-family: var(--mt-mono);
		font-size: 0.85em;
	}
	.mt-pipeline figcaption {
		margin-top: 0.7rem;
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		color: var(--mt-fg-subtle);
	}
	@media (max-width: 44rem) {
		.mt-pipeline__row {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
		.mt-pipeline__stage + .mt-pipeline__stage::before {
			content: '↓';
			left: 50%;
			top: -0.78rem;
			transform: translateX(-50%);
		}
	}
</style>
